# Testing rules

- Tests live in `backend/tests/` and run with `cd backend && python -m pytest` (42 tests).
- Use the `make_world` fixture (`backend/tests/conftest.py`): a gateway, a simulator and a simulated clock on a temporary SQLite database.
- Cover failure and fault-injection paths, not only the happy path.
- A new safeguard needs an ablation test in `test_ablations.py` showing it changes behaviour.
- Fix failing tests before marking work complete; never weaken an assertion to make a test pass.
